WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.172 --> 00:00:01.961
- Tell people what's the funnest moment

00:00:01.961 --> 00:00:02.926
that we've shared together,

00:00:02.926 --> 00:00:04.968
working together, for four years.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:07.224
What's the fun, or
funniest moment, we had?

00:00:07.224 --> 00:00:08.232
- When you graduated.

00:00:08.232 --> 00:00:09.498
- Why was that funny?

00:00:09.498 --> 00:00:12.581
(fun jam band music)

00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:18.553
- Today's the kick off
for National Nurses Week,

00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:21.560
where we honor and
celebrate all the many roles

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:23.844
that nurses play every single day.

00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:26.245
They truly are the backbone and front line

00:00:26.245 --> 00:00:27.652
of the healthcare industry.

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:29.034
Why was that funny?

00:00:29.034 --> 00:00:30.421
- Because I had to give a speech.

00:00:30.421 --> 00:00:31.259
- And what did you say?

00:00:31.259 --> 00:00:32.681
- And Micheal did not get it.

00:00:32.681 --> 00:00:35.515
I said "Right now I could use
a nice, tall White Russian."

00:00:35.515 --> 00:00:37.062
People who got the joke loved it,

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:38.440
but then, you know.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.973
- Well, not everyone's an
alcoholic like you, Ginny.

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.435
- (laughs) Especially my White Russians.

00:00:43.435 --> 00:00:45.834
- As you can tell, I'm
really close with the nurses

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.960
I've been working with
for the past few years.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.262
I truly appreciate the work that they do.

00:00:50.262 --> 00:00:51.332
And that's why I get so mad

00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:53.691
when I watch Grey's
Anatomy, or the Good Doctor,

00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:56.202
and I see that their work is minimized.

00:00:56.202 --> 00:00:57.579
It shouldn't be that way

00:00:57.579 --> 00:00:59.782
and I think nurses deserve more credit.

00:00:59.782 --> 00:01:00.709
All right, Yvette.

00:01:00.709 --> 00:01:02.869
It's late, but I have a question for you.

00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:05.379
What would you think one of your duties

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:07.325
that would surprise other people,

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:08.694
that you do as a nurse?

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:09.772
- Where do you want me to start?

00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:10.605
- I don't know.

00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:11.438
Give me something.

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.722
- The nurse does the
majority of the education

00:01:13.722 --> 00:01:16.139
when it comes to medications,

00:01:17.213 --> 00:01:18.130
wound care,

00:01:19.085 --> 00:01:22.898
and with the vaccines that we
administer to the children.

00:01:22.898 --> 00:01:23.731
- Right.

00:01:23.731 --> 00:01:25.419
When was that last time you
seen a doctor give a vaccine?

00:01:25.419 --> 00:01:27.982
- Only our residents, when
they're making their numbers.

00:01:27.982 --> 00:01:29.001
- Exactly.

00:01:29.001 --> 00:01:29.834
- That's it.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:32.724
- Unless you've been personally
admitted into a hospital,

00:01:32.724 --> 00:01:34.509
or maybe spent time with a loved one

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:36.073
who's been admitted to a hospital,

00:01:36.073 --> 00:01:38.548
it's difficult to know the entire scope

00:01:38.548 --> 00:01:40.636
of what a nurse does day to day.

00:01:40.636 --> 00:01:42.741
And those duties are really remarkable.

00:01:42.741 --> 00:01:44.255
They care for your physical health.

00:01:44.255 --> 00:01:45.907
They care for your emotional health.

00:01:45.907 --> 00:01:48.133
They evaluate how well
your treatment's going.

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:51.190
And something maybe some
doctors are reluctant to say,

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:54.135
but they really do alert
us when we make mistakes.

00:01:54.135 --> 00:01:57.004
In reality, doctors don't
save lives, you save lives.

00:01:57.004 --> 00:01:58.245
- Doctors save lives as well.

00:01:58.245 --> 00:01:59.307
- Well, teamwork.

00:01:59.307 --> 00:02:00.424
- It's absolutely teamwork.

00:02:00.424 --> 00:02:01.257
- Yes.
(smack)

00:02:01.257 --> 00:02:02.090
- Absolutely.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:02.923
- Yay!

00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:05.337
What makes it a lot easier
to get up in the morning

00:02:05.337 --> 00:02:08.568
and come to a 16 hour
shift, or a 12 hour shift,

00:02:08.568 --> 00:02:10.824
is that I have fun with my nurses.

00:02:10.824 --> 00:02:12.325
We have a good time.

00:02:12.325 --> 00:02:14.606
Like, a genuinely good time.

00:02:14.606 --> 00:02:16.106
We're laughing, we're talking,

00:02:16.106 --> 00:02:17.815
we're sharing our experiences.

00:02:17.815 --> 00:02:19.157
I think that ability to take

00:02:19.157 --> 00:02:22.335
a very stressful situation,
a very somber situation,

00:02:22.335 --> 00:02:24.377
and turn it into something light-hearted,

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.960
and fun, and interesting,

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:28.605
is a great quality for a nurse to have.

00:02:28.605 --> 00:02:29.764
Not only for patients,

00:02:29.764 --> 00:02:31.736
but also for other members
of the healthcare team,

00:02:31.736 --> 00:02:32.906
like us doctors.

00:02:32.906 --> 00:02:34.800
Now I know some of you may be in nursing,

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.964
or considering becoming a nurse,

00:02:36.964 --> 00:02:38.709
and there's a couple points I want to make

00:02:38.709 --> 00:02:39.636
about the career.

00:02:39.636 --> 00:02:42.715
It's one of the most noble,
rewarding careers out there.

00:02:42.715 --> 00:02:44.615
It has amazing job security.

00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:47.080
For the next few decades,
the demand for nurses

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.291
is only going to go up and up and up.

00:02:49.291 --> 00:02:52.459
On top of that, you have such
a broad scope of practice.

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:53.881
Meaning you can work in a hospital,

00:02:53.881 --> 00:02:56.132
in the nursing home, in administration.

00:02:56.132 --> 00:02:58.796
The medical world is truly your oyster.

00:02:58.796 --> 00:03:01.178
People are often quick to
write off the nursing field

00:03:01.178 --> 00:03:04.228
based on others' expectations
of what the job is.

00:03:04.228 --> 00:03:06.261
Or, they're quick to love the field

00:03:06.261 --> 00:03:08.645
based on something that
they have overheard,

00:03:08.645 --> 00:03:11.338
or something that they've
projected onto the field.

00:03:11.338 --> 00:03:14.443
I think you really need to
spend some time with a nurse.

00:03:14.443 --> 00:03:17.883
Walk into a hospital,
volunteer at a nursing home.

00:03:17.883 --> 00:03:20.307
Spend some time with nurses to find out

00:03:20.307 --> 00:03:21.814
what they're day to day is like.

00:03:21.814 --> 00:03:23.945
If you're gonna make this your occupation,

00:03:23.945 --> 00:03:25.196
and you're gonna practice this

00:03:25.196 --> 00:03:27.609
for 20, 30, maybe even 40 years,

00:03:27.609 --> 00:03:30.533
you need to know if you
truly love this field or not.

00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:33.328
And the way to find
that out is by diving in

00:03:33.328 --> 00:03:35.046
and stepping outside of your comfort zone.

00:03:35.046 --> 00:03:36.262
So, if they're curious,

00:03:36.262 --> 00:03:38.184
or think that they wanna become a nurse,

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.519
what's a good step for
them to take, preliminary?

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:41.772
Should they just apply right away

00:03:41.772 --> 00:03:43.164
or should they do some more research?

00:03:43.164 --> 00:03:44.900
- I mean, definitely encourage you to try

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.966
to get, you know,
experience on the bedside.

00:03:47.966 --> 00:03:50.620
That develops your assessment skills,

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.122
your communication skills,

00:03:52.122 --> 00:03:54.839
not only with the patient
themselves, but family members.

00:03:54.839 --> 00:03:56.109
- Now, even though I'm a doctor,

00:03:56.109 --> 00:03:59.151
I do have some advice for
aspiring nurses out there.

00:03:59.151 --> 00:04:01.258
Before you take someone else's advice

00:04:01.258 --> 00:04:03.181
of why you shouldn't go into nursing,

00:04:03.181 --> 00:04:05.222
or why you should go into nursing,

00:04:05.222 --> 00:04:06.518
you really need to figure out

00:04:06.518 --> 00:04:08.589
if it's a career that's right for you.

00:04:08.589 --> 00:04:11.326
Being a nurse is a demanding occupation.

00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:14.266
At times you're working
crazy, long shifts.

00:04:14.266 --> 00:04:16.445
Spending that time standing on your feet.

00:04:16.445 --> 00:04:18.235
Sometimes you have to
give up your holidays

00:04:18.235 --> 00:04:20.577
where you would be spending
time with loved ones,

00:04:20.577 --> 00:04:23.401
and instead are taking
care of complete strangers.

00:04:23.401 --> 00:04:25.515
And sometimes, worst of all,

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:28.887
you may not receive the
gratitude you truly deserve,

00:04:28.887 --> 00:04:31.038
both from patients and doctors.

00:04:31.038 --> 00:04:32.733
I've heard this said once before,

00:04:32.733 --> 00:04:34.727
I don't even remember the context,

00:04:34.727 --> 00:04:37.662
but being, and becoming, a nurse is hard.

00:04:37.662 --> 00:04:39.617
But it's the hard that makes it special.

00:04:39.617 --> 00:04:41.208
To all the nurses out there,

00:04:41.208 --> 00:04:42.889
happy Nurse's Week,

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:44.735
and from the bottom of my heart,

00:04:44.735 --> 00:04:45.691
thank you.

00:04:45.691 --> 00:04:46.524
- Thank you.

00:04:46.524 --> 00:04:47.357
- Thank you.

00:04:47.357 --> 00:04:48.190
- Thank you.

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:49.023
- Thank you.

00:04:49.023 --> 00:04:49.856
- Thank you.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:50.689
- Thank you.

00:04:50.689 --> 00:04:51.522
- Thank you.

00:04:51.522 --> 00:04:52.355
- Thank you.

00:04:52.355 --> 00:04:53.188
- Thank you.

00:04:53.188 --> 00:04:54.021
- Thank you.

00:04:54.021 --> 00:04:54.854
- Thank you.

00:04:54.854 --> 00:04:55.935
- Thanks everybody, for all you do.

00:04:55.935 --> 00:04:56.768
(beep)

00:04:56.768 --> 00:04:57.601
- Do you still party?

00:04:57.601 --> 00:04:58.434
I know you party.

00:04:58.434 --> 00:04:59.267
- Micheal.

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.460
(Micheal laughs)

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.393
Go away now.

00:05:01.393 --> 00:05:02.226
- Okay.

00:05:02.226 --> 00:05:05.143
(slow funk music)

